# Fichero Release Notes

## 0.1.0-dev In Progress (July 4, 2025)
- [x] Added new windows for Plans, Projects, and Prompts.
- [x] Refactored Director.py:
  - [x] Refactored director.py into modular components for better maintainability, e.g. backends, cofnig, interfaces, monitoring, and utils.
  - [x] Moved backend to run entirely on Python, making Redis and Celery optional for HPC  environments. 
  - [] Tested REDIS/Celery. 
  - [x] Implemented threading for CPU-intensive tasks when processing a single folder, significantly improving performance.
  - [x] Developed monitoring backends, and added shared data storage for encrypted API keys and settings.
  - [x] Updated tools to be called as function calls instead of subprocesses.

- [x] Redesigned the plans format to remove the Weasel dependency and eliminated the Weasel backend.

- [x] Successfully processed 50 folders (7,992 images) as part of the [Archivo Afro](https://upenn.app.box.com/s/ezpp32x9p0yps244buzweyqfyn67h5l) project.

- [x] In remove_background.py, Integrated rembg for AI-based background removal (optional). If rembg is unavailable, Fichero falls back to contour-based background removal. The GUI disables the AI background removal option on Mac if rembg is not installed, and on other platforms where rembg or scikit-image may not work.

- [x] In crop.py made ultralytics optional for Mac builds. Added a YOLO_AVAILABLE flag to check for YOLO. If YOLO is unavailable, cropping falls back to contour-based methods. crop_with_yolo() returns None if YOLO is not available. crop_batch() now handles YOLO loading more gracefully.

- [x] Revised the Activity Monitor to ensure only one instance can be active at a time.

#### Activity Monitor Improvements (in progress)
- [X] Implement a simple tree view with columns to improve readability and prevent items from being deleted or reordered.

Tasks to Work On:
