## 0.0.5 – JUNE 15, 2025
- [x] Added menus.
- [x] Added user interface translation support.
- [x] Added an Settings window, inspired by BBEdit.
  - [x] Created a settings window that lets you edit API keys for OpenAI and Qwen.
  - [x] Added app settings for API keys. API keys are loaded from environment variables if available; otherwise, they can be set via the Settings window. API keys are saved, encrypted, in the appropriate folder based on the operating system.

## 0.0.4 – JUNE 13, 2025
- [x] Added Briefcase for easier packaging and distribution of Fichero.
- [x] Integrated Toga for macOS, Windows, and Linux GUI development. (About Box GUI inspired by John Siracusa's [Hyperspace](https://hypercritical.co/2025/02/25/hyperspace).)
- [x] Moved files into the `src` directory to support Toga and Briefcase.
- [x] Refactored code to work with Briefcase and Toga.

## 0.0.3 – JUNE 5, 2025
- [x] Added support for multi-step LLM processing using llm_process.py, llm_utils.py, and a config file. (Tested with OpenAI models.)
- [x] Enabled plans files to set prompts, choose batch sizes, decide between sending pages individually or in groups (up to chunk size based on max tokens), combine results, and send previous results.
- [x] Added a plan to auto-catalogue using LLMs for named entity recognition (people, places, organizations, events), as well as specific entities of interest (e.g., mines, animals, plants, injuries), a timeline of events, most important people, ten tags or keywords, and a 150-word summary.

## 0.0.2 – MAY 25, 2025
- [x] Support for running on multiple processors and in parallel, with asynchronous transcription calls (fichero_director.py).

## 0.0.1 – MAY 9, 2025
- [x] Initial development release: supports cropping, splitting, rotating, enhancing, background removal, and transcription.

